      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-14T20:19:26Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, I see that this is addressing a question I had in a previous review. Might be nice if this was pulled back into the base CL to make it a bit more atomic?",
      "revId": "29ec258bb2e8baf546457b3df8096eb2fb1a7a8f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "ab9a78ea_f39618bb",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/BindGroupLayoutInternal.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 467,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-14T20:50:49Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Hmm... So browsing the code a bit, we only really need to keep an entry for each thing because we have `GetBindingInfo` that needs to return the appropriate `BindingInfo`. I\u0027m worried that for large arrays, we are effectively duplicating a ton of data in memory when really, we can compute that information on the fly by having something smaller, maybe a map to the index of the actual `BindingInfo` and then just modifying from there?\n\nI\u0027m also wondering whether `BindingInfo` actually needs to store the `binding` at all since we have to pass in a binding index to get it in the first place? (I\u0027m not as confident about this...), but if not, we could potentially store even less information and reduce our memory footprint?",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 458,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 467,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "29ec258bb2e8baf546457b3df8096eb2fb1a7a8f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "133a562e_e9cf3590",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/BindGroupLayoutInternal.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 467,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-16T17:03:47Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "That\u0027s a valid concern because the memory used will be a larger than it could, however fixed-size arrays should stay relatively small because they still validate against the `max*PerStage` limits. Bindless will be a whole different mechanism.\n\nI didn\u0027t want to add the indirection because bind group creation is very hot code that needs to look up each BindingInfo at least twice (once (or twice) in frontend validation and once in the backend). Adding a random access indirection seems like it would be much worse than using more memory (and cache lines) for the BGL, in the semi-rare case where fixed binding_array are used. WDYT?",
      "parentUuid": "ab9a78ea_f39618bb",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 458,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 467,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "29ec258bb2e8baf546457b3df8096eb2fb1a7a8f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "3144cd2d_22245e70",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/BindGroupLayoutInternal.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 467,
      "author": {
        "id": 1002831
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-16T20:32:35Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "Ah, that makes sense and means that the max length of this is much smaller given the `max*PerStage` limits! I did in fact confuse this with Bindless and was concerned with much large values in these arrays, thereby causing a huge memory footprint.\n\nThat said, do you know if my second point about whether `BindingInfo` needing to store `binding` is true? If so, we could maybe at least make it so that we have one `vector\u003cBindingInfo\u003e` and one `ityp::vector\u003cBindingIndex, BindingInfo*\u003e` such that the first one stores the actual backing `BindingInfo`s and the second one is the dense one that stores a pointer for each index?\n\nI don\u0027t feel too strongly about that optimization now though, given that the limits all added together is \u003c 64 in the default case. So leave it up to you to decide if we need it or not.",
      "parentUuid": "133a562e_e9cf3590",
      "range": {
        "startLine": 458,
        "startChar": 8,
        "endLine": 467,
        "endChar": 9
      },
      "revId": "29ec258bb2e8baf546457b3df8096eb2fb1a7a8f",
      "serverId": "dd02978d-1a8e-36d7-bcc0-a5723e5c0abd"
    },
    {
      "unresolved": true,
      "key": {
        "uuid": "cf4f2b69_0a5b0a16",
        "filename": "src/dawn/native/BindGroupLayoutInternal.cpp",
        "patchSetId": 3
      },
      "lineNbr": 467,
      "author": {
        "id": 1000002
      },
      "writtenOn": "2025-04-17T11:35:52Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "I\u0027ll open an issue about it, yeah the BindingNumber is used in a few places (some shader modules, in the production of the helpful error message for BGs with unverified buffers sizes being bound) but only cold code so it makes sense to separate it.\n\nAnd I agree that we could use even smaller integer types to save memory and cache lines. That said I don\u0027t think that we should do the double indirection even in this case because implementation of fixed-size binding array should not slow down regular BG creation.",
      "parentUuid": "3144cd2d_22245e70",
      "range": {
